/-!
# The étale topology is finer than the one generated by Zariski and finite étale covers

Let `X` be a smooth connected affine curve over `ℂ` and `g : Y ⟶ X` a finite morphism of degree
`3` from a smooth connected curve, with a point `x` whose fibre `g⁻¹(x) = {u, y}` consists of an
unramified point `u` and a point `y` of ramification index `2`, and such that `g` is unramified
away from `y`. Then the étale cover `U = Y ∖ {y} ⟶ X` is not refined by any finite composition
of open immersions and finite étale morphisms ([Stacks, Tag 0HAR]).

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.not_exists_cover_zariskiFiniteEtale_lift`: Tag 0HAR.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleNotZariskiFiniteEtale.not_mem_range_of_zariskiFiniteEtaleTower`: the
  pointwise form, no such composition lifting to `U` has a point over `x`.

## Proof

The proof is the source's. For a scheme `W` étale over `X` and a point `w` over `x`, consider
the part of `Y ×_X W` over the connected component of `w`; the invariant
`AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleNotZariskiFiniteEtale.PreconnectedOverComponent` asks that it be
preconnected (the source's `n = 1`). It holds for `X` itself, since `Y` is connected.

* It passes to open subschemes: `Y ×_X W` is smooth over `ℂ`, hence normal, so a preconnected open
  subset of it is irreducible and its nonempty open subsets stay preconnected.
* It passes along finite étale morphisms `W' ⟶ W`: a splitting of the part over a component of
  `W'` into two open and closed pieces gives, by counting the two points over `w'`, a piece whose
  only point over `w'` lies over `u`. That piece is finite flat of rank `1` over the component,
  hence isomorphic to it, and the induced map from the component to `Y ×_X W` has open and closed
  image avoiding every point over `y`. This is impossible, since that image contains the
  preconnected part over the component of the image of `w'`, which meets the fibre over `y`.
* At the top of the tower a lift `W ⟶ U` is a section of `Y ×_X W ⟶ W` with open and closed image
  avoiding the points over `y`, which contradicts the invariant in the same way.

The ramification enters only through
`AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleNotZariskiFiniteEtale.false_of_etale_comp_of_le_sq`: an `X`-morphism from
a scheme étale over `X` never meets `y`, because `𝔪_x 𝒪_{Y,y} ⊆ 𝔪_y ^ 2`. The two fibre points
over `w'` are distinct and unique because all the residue fields involved are `ℂ`.

## Implementation notes

The finite compositions of open immersions and finite étale morphisms are the
`CategoryTheory.MorphismProperty.multiplicativeClosure` of the class
`@IsOpenImmersion ⊔ (@IsFinite ⊓ @Etale)`. The degree of `g` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.degreeOver` ([Stacks, Tag 02NY]) and the ramification indices are those of
the local rings, `Stacks.DiscreteValuationRing.Ramification.ramificationIdx`; the hypothesis that
`g` is unramified away from `y` is formal unramifiedness of the restriction of `g` to `U`. The
degree and the ramification index at `u` are part of the source's setup but are not used by the
proof: the count of the two points of each fibre over `x` replaces the degree count.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0HAR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0HAR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0HAQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0HAQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits IsLocalRing

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleNotZariskiFiniteEtale

/-- A formally unramified morphism locally of finite type induces a bijection on residue fields
at every point whose image has an algebraically closed residue field: the residue field
extension is separable, hence algebraic, hence trivial. -/
theorem residueFieldMap_bijective_of_isAlgClosed {T S : Scheme.{u}} (φ : T ⟶ S)
    [FormallyUnramified φ] [LocallyOfFiniteType φ] (t : T)
    [IsAlgClosed (S.residueField (φ t))] :
    Function.Bijective (φ.residueFieldMap t).hom := by
  let : Algebra (S.residueField (φ t)) (T.residueField t) := (φ.residueFieldMap t).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Algebra.IsSeparable (S.residueField (φ t)) (T.residueField t) := inferInstance
  exact IsAlgClosed.algebraMap_bijective_of_isIntegral

/-- In a Noetherian local ring, `𝔪 ≤ 𝔪 ^ 2` forces `𝔪 = 0` (Nakayama). -/
theorem maximalIdeal_eq_bot_of_le_sq (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (h : maximalIdeal R ≤ maximalIdeal R ^ 2) : maximalIdeal R = ⊥ :=
  Submodule.eq_bot_of_le_smul_of_le_jacobson_bot (maximalIdeal R) (maximalIdeal R)
    (IsNoetherian.noetherian _) (by rwa [sq, ← Ideal.smul_eq_mul] at h)
    (jacobson_eq_maximalIdeal ⊥ bot_ne_top).ge

/-- **A morphism étale over the base cannot pass through a ramified point.** Let `g : Y ⟶ X` and
`h : T ⟶ Y` be morphisms with `h ≫ g` étale and `T` locally Noetherian. If at the point `h t` the
maximal ideal of `𝒪_{X, g (h t)}` generates an ideal contained in `𝔪_{h t} ^ 2` and
`𝒪_{X, g (h t)}` is not a field, there is a contradiction: the composite stalk map is
unramified, so `𝔪_t = 𝔪_X 𝒪_{T,t} ⊆ 𝔪_t ^ 2`, whence `𝒪_{T,t}` is a field by Nakayama, and the
flat local map `𝒪_{X, g (h t)} → 𝒪_{T,t}` is injective. -/
theorem false_of_etale_comp_of_le_sq {T Y X : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) (h : T ⟶ Y)
    [Etale (h ≫ g)] [IsLocallyNoetherian T] (t : T)
    (hram : Ideal.map (g.stalkMap (h t)).hom (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t)))) ≤
      maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (h t)) ^ 2)
    (hnf : ¬ IsField (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t)))) : False := by
  set φ := (g.stalkMap (h t)).hom
  set ψ := (h.stalkMap t).hom
  have hcomp : ((h ≫ g).stalkMap t).hom = ψ.comp φ := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.stalkMap_comp]; rfl
  have hfu : ((h ≫ g).stalkMap t).hom.FormallyUnramified := FormallyUnramified.stalkMap _ t
  have hft : ((h ≫ g).stalkMap t).hom.EssFiniteType := LocallyOfFiniteType.stalkMap _ t
  have hfl : ((h ≫ g).stalkMap t).hom.Flat := Flat.stalkMap _ t
  rw [hcomp] at hfu hft hfl
  let : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t))) (T.presheaf.stalk t) := (ψ.comp φ).toAlgebra
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t))) (T.presheaf.stalk t)) :=
    inferInstanceAs (IsLocalHom (ψ.comp φ))
  have : Algebra.FormallyUnramified (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t))) (T.presheaf.stalk t) := hfu
  have : Algebra.EssFiniteType (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t))) (T.presheaf.stalk t) := hft
  have : Module.Flat (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t))) (T.presheaf.stalk t) := hfl
  have hmap := Algebra.FormallyUnramified.map_maximalIdeal
    (R := X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t))) (S := T.presheaf.stalk t)
  have hψ : Ideal.map ψ (maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (h t))) ≤
      maximalIdeal (T.presheaf.stalk t) :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun a ha => (map_mem_nonunits_iff ψ a).mpr ha
  have hle' : Ideal.map (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t))) (T.presheaf.stalk t))
      (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t)))) ≤ maximalIdeal (T.presheaf.stalk t) ^ 2 := by
    change Ideal.map (ψ.comp φ) _ ≤ _
    rw [← Ideal.map_map]
    calc Ideal.map ψ (Ideal.map φ (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t)))))
        ≤ Ideal.map ψ (maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (h t)) ^ 2) := Ideal.map_mono hram
      _ = Ideal.map ψ (maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk (h t))) ^ 2 := Ideal.map_pow _ _ _
      _ ≤ _ := Ideal.pow_right_mono hψ 2
  have hle : maximalIdeal (T.presheaf.stalk t) ≤ maximalIdeal (T.presheaf.stalk t) ^ 2 := by
    rwa [hmap] at hle'
  have hbot := maximalIdeal_eq_bot_of_le_sq _ hle
  have : Module.FaithfullyFlat (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t))) (T.presheaf.stalk t) :=
    Module.FaithfullyFlat.of_flat_of_isLocalHom
  have hinj := FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t))) (T.presheaf.stalk t)
  refine hnf ((isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq).mpr (eq_bot_iff.mpr fun a ha => ?_))
  have : algebraMap _ (T.presheaf.stalk t) a ∈ maximalIdeal (T.presheaf.stalk t) := by
    rw [← hmap]; exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ ha
  rw [hbot, Ideal.mem_bot, ← map_zero (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk (g (h t)))
    (T.presheaf.stalk t))] at this
  exact (Ideal.mem_bot).mpr (hinj this)

/-- If the residue field map at the first point of a triplet is bijective, the fibre of the
pullback over that triplet is a single point. -/
theorem subsingleton_spec_tensor {X Y S : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ S} {g : Y ⟶ S}
    (T : Scheme.Pullback.Triplet f g) (hbij : Function.Bijective (f.residueFieldMap T.x).hom) :
    Subsingleton (Spec T.tensor) := by
  have : IsIso (f.residueFieldMap T.x) := (ConcreteCategory.isIso_iff_bijective _).mpr hbij
  have : IsIso (pushout.inr ((S.residueFieldCongr T.hx).inv ≫ f.residueFieldMap T.x)
      ((S.residueFieldCongr T.hy).inv ≫ g.residueFieldMap T.y)) := inferInstance
  have hinj : Function.Injective (Spec.map (pushout.inr
      ((S.residueFieldCongr T.hx).inv ≫ f.residueFieldMap T.x)
      ((S.residueFieldCongr T.hy).inv ≫ g.residueFieldMap T.y))).base :=
    (Scheme.homeoOfIso (asIso (Spec.map _))).injective
  exact ⟨fun a b => hinj (Subsingleton.elim _ _)⟩

/-- Two points of a fibre product with the same images in both factors coincide, provided the
residue field extension at the first image is trivial. -/
theorem pullback_point_eq {X Y S : Scheme.{u}} {f : X ⟶ S} {g : Y ⟶ S}
    (t₁ t₂ : ↑(pullback f g)) (h₁ : pullback.fst f g t₁ = pullback.fst f g t₂)
    (h₂ : pullback.snd f g t₁ = pullback.snd f g t₂)
    (hbij : Function.Bijective (f.residueFieldMap (pullback.fst f g t₂)).hom) : t₁ = t₂ := by
  apply Scheme.Pullback.carrierEquiv.injective
  rw [Scheme.Pullback.carrierEquiv_eq_iff]
  have e : Scheme.Pullback.Triplet.ofPoint t₁ = Scheme.Pullback.Triplet.ofPoint t₂ :=
    Scheme.Pullback.Triplet.ext h₁ h₂
  refine ⟨e, ?_⟩
  have : Subsingleton (Spec (Scheme.Pullback.carrierEquiv t₂).1.tensor) :=
    subsingleton_spec_tensor (Scheme.Pullback.carrierEquiv t₂).1 hbij
  exact Subsingleton.elim _ _

section ClosedPoints

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]

/-- The residue field of a closed point of a scheme locally of finite type over an algebraically
closed field `k` is algebraically closed: it is a finite extension of `k`, hence `k` itself. -/
theorem isAlgClosed_residueField_of_isClosed {S : Scheme.{u}} (π : S ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [LocallyOfFiniteType π] (s : S) (hs : IsClosed ({s} : Set S)) :
    IsAlgClosed (S.residueField s) := by
  let : Algebra k (S.residueField s) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ π.appTop ≫ S.Γevaluation s).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Module.Finite k (S.residueField s) := residueField_finite_of_closed_point k π s hs
  exact IsAlgClosed.of_ringEquiv k _
    (RingEquiv.ofBijective _ (IsAlgClosed.algebraMap_bijective_of_isIntegral (k := k)))

/-- A morphism over an algebraically closed field `k` between schemes locally of finite type
over `k` induces a bijection on the residue fields of a closed point and of its closed image:
both are `k`. -/
theorem residueFieldMap_bijective_of_isClosed {S T : Scheme.{u}} (πS : S ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    (πT : T ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [LocallyOfFiniteType πS] [LocallyOfFiniteType πT] (φ : T ⟶ S)
    (hφ : φ ≫ πS = πT) (t : T) (ht : IsClosed ({t} : Set T)) (hs : IsClosed ({φ t} : Set S)) :
    Function.Bijective (φ.residueFieldMap t).hom := by
  let : Algebra k (S.residueField (φ t)) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ πS.appTop ≫ S.Γevaluation (φ t)).hom.toAlgebra
  let : Algebra k (T.residueField t) :=
    ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ πT.appTop ≫ T.Γevaluation t).hom.toAlgebra
  have : Module.Finite k (S.residueField (φ t)) := residueField_finite_of_closed_point k πS _ hs
  have : Module.Finite k (T.residueField t) := residueField_finite_of_closed_point k πT t ht
  have hS : Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (S.residueField (φ t))) :=
    IsAlgClosed.algebraMap_bijective_of_isIntegral
  have hT : Function.Bijective (algebraMap k (T.residueField t)) :=
    IsAlgClosed.algebraMap_bijective_of_isIntegral
  have hfac : algebraMap k (T.residueField t) =
      (φ.residueFieldMap t).hom.comp (algebraMap k (S.residueField (φ t))) := by
    change ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ πT.appTop ≫ T.Γevaluation t).hom =
      ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ πS.appTop ≫ S.Γevaluation (φ t) ≫
        φ.residueFieldMap t).hom
    rw [Scheme.Γevaluation_naturality, ← hφ, Scheme.Hom.comp_appTop]
    simp only [Category.assoc]
  rw [hfac, RingHom.coe_comp] at hT
  exact (Function.Bijective.of_comp_iff _ hS).mp hT

end ClosedPoints

section Tower

/-- The class of finite compositions of open immersions and finite étale morphisms. -/
abbrev zariskiFiniteEtaleTower : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u} :=
  (@IsOpenImmersion ⊔ (@IsFinite ⊓ @Etale) : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}).multiplicativeClosure

/-- A finite composition of open immersions and finite étale morphisms is étale. -/
theorem etale_of_zariskiFiniteEtaleTower {W X : Scheme.{u}} {p : W ⟶ X}
    (hp : zariskiFiniteEtaleTower p) : Etale p := by
  induction hp with
  | of f hf =>
    rcases hf with hf | hf
    · have : IsOpenImmersion f := hf
      infer_instance
    · exact hf.2
  | id x => infer_instance
  | comp_of f g _ hg ih =>
    have : Etale g := by
      rcases hg with hg | hg
      · have : IsOpenImmersion g := hg
        infer_instance
      · exact hg.2
    infer_instance

/-- The source of an open immersion or of a finite morphism into a Noetherian scheme is
Noetherian. -/
theorem isNoetherian_of_step {W W' : Scheme.{u}} (q : W' ⟶ W) [IsNoetherian W]
    (hq : (@IsOpenImmersion ⊔ (@IsFinite ⊓ @Etale) : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) q) :
    IsNoetherian W' := by
  rcases hq with hq | hq
  · have : IsOpenImmersion q := hq
    have : IsLocallyNoetherian W' := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian q
    have hc : IsCompact (Set.range q) :=
      TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace.isCompact _
    have : CompactSpace W' := by
      rw [← isCompact_univ_iff, q.isOpenEmbedding.isInducing.isCompact_iff, Set.image_univ]
      exact hc
    exact { }
  · have : IsFinite q := hq.1
    have : IsLocallyNoetherian W' := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian q
    have : CompactSpace W' := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace q
    exact { }

end Tower

section Avoid

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) (U : Y.Opens)

/-- The part of `Y ×_X W` lying over `U ⊆ Y` is the base change of `U ⟶ X` along `W ⟶ X`. -/
theorem isPullback_restrict_fst {W : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) :
    IsPullback (pullback.fst U.ι (pullback.fst g p))
      (pullback.snd U.ι (pullback.fst g p) ≫ pullback.snd g p) (U.ι ≫ g) p :=
  (IsPullback.of_hasPullback _ _).paste_vert (IsPullback.of_hasPullback g p)

/-- **Images of sections étale over the base avoiding the branch locus are open.** Let
`p : W ⟶ X`, let `t : T ⟶ W` be étale and let `σ : T ⟶ Y ×_X W` lie over `t`. If `σ` lands
over the open `U ⊆ Y` on which `g` is unramified, then `σ` has open image: it factors through
`U ×_X W`, which is unramified over `W`, so it is étale. -/
theorem isOpen_range_of_mem {W T : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) [FormallyUnramified (U.ι ≫ g)]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (U.ι ≫ g)] (t : T ⟶ W) [Etale t] (σ : T ⟶ pullback g p)
    (hσ : σ ≫ pullback.snd g p = t) (hmem : ∀ c, pullback.fst g p (σ c) ∈ U) :
    IsOpen (Set.range σ) := by
  set a := pullback.snd U.ι (pullback.fst g p)
  have hsub : Set.range σ ⊆ Set.range a := by
    rintro _ ⟨c, rfl⟩
    rw [Scheme.Pullback.range_snd, Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    exact hmem c
  set σ₀ := IsOpenImmersion.lift a σ hsub
  have hfac : σ₀ ≫ a = σ := IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac a σ hsub
  have hpb := isPullback_restrict_fst g U p
  have : FormallyUnramified (a ≫ pullback.snd g p) :=
    MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (P := @FormallyUnramified) hpb ‹_›
  have : LocallyOfFiniteType (a ≫ pullback.snd g p) :=
    MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (P := @LocallyOfFiniteType) hpb ‹_›
  have : Etale (σ₀ ≫ a ≫ pullback.snd g p) := by
    rw [← Category.assoc, hfac, hσ]; infer_instance
  have : Etale σ₀ := Etale.of_comp σ₀ (a ≫ pullback.snd g p)
  have hrange : Set.range σ = a '' Set.range σ₀ := by
    rw [← Set.range_comp]
    congr 1
    funext c
    rw [Function.comp_apply, ← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hfac]
  rw [hrange]
  exact a.isOpenEmbedding.isOpenMap _ σ₀.isOpenMap.isOpen_range

end Avoid

section Core

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) (U : Y.Opens) (x : X)

/-- For `p : W ⟶ X`, the property that over the connected component of every point `w` of `W`
lying over `x`, the fibre product `Y ×_X W` is preconnected. This is the condition `n = 1` of the
source's proof, read on the connected component of the point. -/
def PreconnectedOverComponent {W : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) : Prop :=
  ∀ w : W, p w = x → _root_.IsPreconnected ((pullback.snd g p) ⁻¹' connectedComponent w)

/-- The images of a point of `Y ×_X W` in `X` agree. -/
theorem pullback_condition_apply {W : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) (z : ↥(pullback g p)) :
    g (pullback.fst g p z) = p (pullback.snd g p z) := by
  rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, pullback.condition, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply]

/-- The base change of `Y ×_X W ⟶ W` along `q : W' ⟶ W` is `Y ×_X W' ⟶ W'`. -/
theorem isPullback_map_snd {W W' : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) (q : W' ⟶ W) :
    IsPullback (pullback.map g (q ≫ p) g p (𝟙 Y) q (𝟙 X) (by simp) (by simp))
      (pullback.snd g (q ≫ p)) (pullback.snd g p) q := by
  have e₁ : pullback.map g (q ≫ p) g p (𝟙 Y) q (𝟙 X) (by simp) (by simp) ≫ pullback.fst g p =
      pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) :=
    (pullback.lift_fst _ _ _).trans (Category.comp_id _)
  have e₂ : pullback.map g (q ≫ p) g p (𝟙 Y) q (𝟙 X) (by simp) (by simp) ≫ pullback.snd g p =
      pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) ≫ q :=
    pullback.lift_snd _ _ _
  refine IsPullback.of_right ?_ e₂ (IsPullback.of_hasPullback g p)
  rw [e₁]
  exact IsPullback.of_hasPullback g (q ≫ p)

/-- A morphism `j : T ⟶ Y ×_X W` which is étale and lands over `U`, on which `g` is étale, is
étale over `W`. -/
theorem etale_comp_snd_of_mem {W T : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) [Etale (U.ι ≫ g)]
    (j : T ⟶ pullback g p) [Etale j] (hmem : ∀ c, pullback.fst g p (j c) ∈ U) :
    Etale (j ≫ pullback.snd g p) := by
  set a := pullback.snd U.ι (pullback.fst g p)
  have hsub : Set.range j ⊆ Set.range a := by
    rintro _ ⟨c, rfl⟩
    rw [Scheme.Pullback.range_snd, Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    exact hmem c
  have hfac : IsOpenImmersion.lift a j hsub ≫ a = j := IsOpenImmersion.lift_fac a j hsub
  have : Etale (a ≫ pullback.snd g p) :=
    MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (P := @Etale) (isPullback_restrict_fst g U p) ‹_›
  have : Etale (IsOpenImmersion.lift a j hsub ≫ a) := by rw [hfac]; infer_instance
  have : Etale (IsOpenImmersion.lift a j hsub) := Etale.of_comp _ a
  rw [← hfac, Category.assoc]
  infer_instance

/-- Over the identity of `X`, the invariant holds as soon as `X` and `Y` are connected. -/
theorem preconnectedOverComponent_id [PreconnectedSpace X] [PreconnectedSpace Y] :
    PreconnectedOverComponent g x (𝟙 X) := by
  intro w _
  rw [PreconnectedSpace.connectedComponent_eq_univ, Set.preimage_univ]
  have hs : Function.Surjective (inv (pullback.fst g (𝟙 X))) :=
    (Scheme.homeoOfIso (asIso (inv (pullback.fst g (𝟙 X))))).surjective
  rw [← hs.range_eq]
  exact isPreconnected_range (inv (pullback.fst g (𝟙 X))).continuous

/-- In a Noetherian scheme smooth over a field, an open preconnected subset is preirreducible:
as an open subscheme it is connected, normal and Noetherian, hence irreducible. -/
theorem isPreirreducible_of_isPreconnected {k : Type u} [Field k] {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (π : Z ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [Smooth π] [IsNoetherian Z] {E : Set Z} (hE : IsOpen E)
    (hc : _root_.IsPreconnected E) : IsPreirreducible E := by
  rcases E.eq_empty_or_nonempty with rfl | hne
  · exact isPreirreducible_empty
  let O : Z.Opens := ⟨E, hE⟩
  have : ConnectedSpace O := isConnected_iff_connectedSpace.mp ⟨hne, hc⟩
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian O := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (O.ι ≫ π)
  have : CompactSpace O :=
    isCompact_iff_compactSpace.mp (TopologicalSpace.NoetherianSpace.isCompact E)
  have : IsNoetherian O := { }
  have : IrreducibleSpace O :=
    irreducibleSpace_of_isNormal_of_connectedSpace O (isNormal_of_smooth_over_field (O.ι ≫ π))
  have := (IrreducibleSpace.isIrreducible_univ O).image O.ι O.ι.continuous.continuousOn
  rw [Set.image_univ, Scheme.Opens.range_ι] at this
  exact this.isPreirreducible

/-- **The invariant passes to an open subscheme.** The part of `Y ×_X W` over a connected
component of `W` is open and preconnected, hence irreducible as `Y ×_X W` is smooth over `k`;
the part over a connected component of an open of `W` is a nonempty open subset of it. -/
theorem preconnectedOverComponent_comp_isOpenImmersion {k : Type u} [Field k]
    (πY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [Smooth πY] [IsFinite g] {W W' : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) [Etale p]
    [IsNoetherian W] (i : W' ⟶ W) [IsOpenImmersion i] (h : PreconnectedOverComponent g x p) :
    PreconnectedOverComponent g x (i ≫ p) := by
  intro w' hw'
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian W' := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian i
  have hpb := isPullback_map_snd g p i
  have : IsOpenImmersion (pullback.map g (i ≫ p) g p (𝟙 Y) i (𝟙 X) (by simp) (by simp)) :=
    MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (P := @IsOpenImmersion) hpb.flip ‹_›
  have hE := h (i w') hw'
  have hEopen : IsOpen ((pullback.snd g p) ⁻¹' connectedComponent (i w')) :=
    isOpen_connectedComponent.preimage (pullback.snd g p).continuous
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian (pullback g p) :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (pullback.snd g p)
  have : CompactSpace ↥(pullback g p) :=
    QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (pullback.snd g p)
  have : IsNoetherian (pullback g p) := { }
  have hirr := isPreirreducible_of_isPreconnected (pullback.fst g p ≫ πY) hEopen hE
  have himg := Scheme.image_preimage_eq_of_isPullback hpb.flip (connectedComponent w')
  have hsub : (pullback.snd g p) ⁻¹' (i '' connectedComponent w') ⊆
      (pullback.snd g p) ⁻¹' connectedComponent (i w') :=
    Set.preimage_mono ((isPreconnected_connectedComponent.image _
      i.continuous.continuousOn).subset_connectedComponent
        (Set.mem_image_of_mem _ mem_connectedComponent))
  have hopen : IsOpen ((pullback.snd g p) ⁻¹' (i '' connectedComponent w')) :=
    (i.isOpenEmbedding.isOpenMap _ isOpen_connectedComponent).preimage (pullback.snd g p).continuous
  have := (hirr.open_subset hopen hsub).isPreconnected
  rw [← himg] at this
  exact (Scheme.Hom.isOpenEmbedding _).isInducing.isPreconnected_image.mp this

end Core

section FiniteEtaleStep

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) (U : Y.Opens) (x : X) (u y : Y)

/-- A point whose residue field maps bijectively onto that of an algebraically closed point has
an algebraically closed residue field. -/
theorem isAlgClosed_residueField_of_bijective {T S : Scheme.{u}} (φ : T ⟶ S) (t : T)
    [IsAlgClosed (S.residueField (φ t))] (hb : Function.Bijective (φ.residueFieldMap t).hom) :
    IsAlgClosed (T.residueField t) :=
  IsAlgClosed.of_ringEquiv _ _ (RingEquiv.ofBijective _ hb)

/-- The étale-over-the-base version of `false_of_etale_comp_of_le_sq`, at a named point. -/
theorem false_of_etale_comp_of_eq {T : Scheme.{u}} (h : T ⟶ Y) [Etale (h ≫ g)]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian T] (t : T) (y' : Y) (hy' : h t = y')
    (hram : Ideal.map (g.stalkMap y').hom (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (g y'))) ≤
      maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk y') ^ 2)
    (hnf : ¬ IsField (X.presheaf.stalk (g y'))) : False := by
  subst hy'
  exact false_of_etale_comp_of_le_sq g h t hram hnf

variable {x u y} in
/-- **The finite étale step, given a piece of degree one.** Suppose that the invariant holds
for `p : W ⟶ X`, let `q : W' ⟶ W` be finite étale, let `w'` lie over `x`, and let `P` be an open
and closed subset of `Y ×_X W'` over the connected component of `w'` whose only point over `w'`
lies over the unramified point. Then `P` has degree `1` over that component, so the component
maps to `Y ×_X W` with open and closed image over a point of `U`; that image then contains the
whole part of `Y ×_X W` over the component of `q w'`, including a point over `y`, which an étale
`X`-scheme cannot reach. -/
theorem false_of_isClopen_piece (hU : (U : Set Y) = {y}ᶜ) (hgy : g y = x) [Etale (U.ι ≫ g)]
    [Flat g] [IsFinite g] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (hram : Ideal.map (g.stalkMap y).hom (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))) ≤
      maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ^ 2)
    (hnf : ¬ IsField (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))) [IsAlgClosed (X.residueField x)]
    {W W' : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) [Etale p] (q : W' ⟶ W) [IsFinite q] [Etale q]
    (h : PreconnectedOverComponent g x p) (w' : W') (hw' : p (q w') = x)
    (P : Set ↥(pullback g (q ≫ p))) (hP : IsClopen P)
    (hPE : P ⊆ (pullback.snd g (q ≫ p)) ⁻¹' connectedComponent w')
    (v' : ↥(pullback g (q ≫ p))) (hv'P : v' ∈ P) (hv' : pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) v' = w')
    (hv'y : pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) v' ≠ y)
    (huniq : ∀ c ∈ P, pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) c = w' → c = v') : False := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian W := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian p
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian W' := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (q ≫ p)
  have hyc : IsClosed ({y} : Set Y) := by
    rw [← compl_compl ({y} : Set Y), ← hU]
    exact U.isOpen.isClosed_compl
  -- `P` as an open subscheme, and its projection `φ` to `W'`
  let PO : (pullback g (q ≫ p)).Opens := ⟨P, hP.isOpen⟩
  have : IsClosedImmersion PO.ι :=
    IsClosedImmersion.of_isPreimmersion _ (by rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι]; exact hP.isClosed)
  set φ := PO.ι ≫ pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) with hφ
  -- the branch part of `P` and its image
  set N := P ∩ pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) ⁻¹' {y}
  have hN : IsClosed N := hP.isClosed.inter (hyc.preimage (pullback.fst g (q ≫ p)).continuous)
  have hM : IsClosed (pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) '' N) :=
    (pullback.snd g (q ≫ p)).isClosedMap _ hN
  have hw'M : w' ∉ pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) '' N := by
    rintro ⟨c, ⟨hcP, hcy⟩, hc⟩
    exact hv'y (huniq c hcP hc ▸ hcy)
  let V : W'.Opens := ⟨(pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) '' N)ᶜ, hM.isOpen_compl⟩
  have hw'V : w' ∈ V := hw'M
  -- over `V`, the projection of `P` is finite étale
  have hjmem : ∀ c : (φ ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme,
      pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) (((φ ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ PO.ι) c) ∈ U := by
    intro c
    have hc : φ ((φ ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι c) ∈ V := c.2
    change pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) (PO.ι ((φ ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι c)) ∈ (U : Set Y)
    rw [hU]
    intro hcy
    exact hc ⟨_, ⟨((φ ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι c).2, hcy⟩, rfl⟩
  have : Etale (((φ ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ PO.ι) ≫ pullback.snd g (q ≫ p)) :=
    etale_comp_snd_of_mem g U (q ≫ p) _ hjmem
  have : Etale ((φ ∣_ V) ≫ V.ι) := by
    rw [morphismRestrict_ι]
    simpa only [φ, Category.assoc] using this
  have : Etale (φ ∣_ V) := Etale.of_comp (φ ∣_ V) V.ι
  -- the unique point over `w'`
  have hv'V : φ ⟨v', hv'P⟩ ∈ V := by
    change pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) v' ∈ V
    rw [hv']
    exact hw'V
  let xV : (φ ⁻¹ᵁ V).toScheme := ⟨⟨v', hv'P⟩, hv'V⟩
  have hφVx : V.ι ((φ ∣_ V) xV) = w' := by
    change ((φ ∣_ V) xV).1 = w'
    rw [morphismRestrict_base_coe]
    exact hv'
  have hfiber : (φ ∣_ V) ⁻¹' {(φ ∣_ V) xV} = {xV} := by
    ext c
    simp only [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
    refine ⟨fun hc => ?_, fun hc => hc ▸ rfl⟩
    have h1 : pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) c.1.1 = w' := by
      have := congrArg V.ι hc
      rw [hφVx] at this
      change ((φ ∣_ V) c).1 = w' at this
      rw [morphismRestrict_base_coe] at this
      exact this
    have h2 := huniq _ c.1.2 h1
    exact Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext h2)
  -- the residue field extension at that point is trivial
  have hxV : (V.ι ≫ q ≫ p) ((φ ∣_ V) xV) = x := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hφVx]
    exact hw'
  have : IsAlgClosed (X.residueField ((V.ι ≫ q ≫ p) ((φ ∣_ V) xV))) := by
    rw [hxV]; infer_instance
  have : IsAlgClosed (V.toScheme.residueField ((φ ∣_ V) xV)) :=
    isAlgClosed_residueField_of_bijective (V.ι ≫ q ≫ p) _
      (residueFieldMap_bijective_of_isAlgClosed (V.ι ≫ q ≫ p) _)
  have hsurj := (residueFieldMap_bijective_of_isAlgClosed (φ ∣_ V) xV).2
  -- so the rank of `φ` at `w'` is one
  have hiso := isIso_fiberToSpecResidueField_of_preimage_singleton (φ ∣_ V) xV hfiber hsurj
  have hrankV : (φ ∣_ V).finrank ((φ ∣_ V) xV) = 1 := by
    have key : ((φ ∣_ V).fiberToSpecResidueField ((φ ∣_ V) xV)).finrank = 1 :=
      Scheme.Hom.finrank_eq_one_of_isIso _
    have hpb := Scheme.Hom.finrank_pullback_snd (φ ∣_ V)
      (V.toScheme.fromSpecResidueField ((φ ∣_ V) xV))
      (default : Spec (V.toScheme.residueField ((φ ∣_ V) xV)))
    rw [Scheme.fromSpecResidueField_apply] at hpb
    rw [← hpb]
    exact congrFun key default
  have hrank : φ.finrank w' = 1 := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.finrank_of_isPullback _ _ _ _ (isPullback_morphismRestrict φ V).flip,
      hφVx] at hrankV
    exact hrankV
  -- hence on the connected component of `w'` the projection of `P` is an isomorphism
  let C : W'.Opens := ⟨connectedComponent w', isOpen_connectedComponent⟩
  have hC1 : ∀ c ∈ connectedComponent w', φ.finrank c = 1 := fun c hc =>
    (φ.isLocallyConstant_finrank.apply_eq_of_isPreconnected isPreconnected_connectedComponent hc
      mem_connectedComponent).trans hrank
  have : IsIso (φ ∣_ C) := by
    rw [Scheme.Hom.isIso_iff_finrank_eq]
    funext c
    rw [Scheme.Hom.finrank_of_isPullback _ _ _ _ (isPullback_morphismRestrict φ C).flip]
    exact hC1 _ c.2
  -- the induced map from the component to `Y ×_X W`
  have hpb := isPullback_map_snd g p q
  set Φ := pullback.map g (q ≫ p) g p (𝟙 Y) q (𝟙 X) (by simp) (by simp)
  have : IsFinite Φ := MorphismProperty.of_isPullback (P := @IsFinite) hpb.flip ‹_›
  set σ := inv (φ ∣_ C) ≫ (φ ⁻¹ᵁ C).ι ≫ PO.ι ≫ Φ with hσdef
  have hσ : σ ≫ pullback.snd g p = C.ι ≫ q := by
    have : (φ ⁻¹ᵁ C).ι ≫ PO.ι ≫ Φ ≫ pullback.snd g p = (φ ∣_ C) ≫ C.ι ≫ q := by
      rw [hpb.w, ← Category.assoc (φ ∣_ C), morphismRestrict_ι]
      simp only [φ, Category.assoc]
    simp only [σ, Category.assoc, this, IsIso.inv_hom_id_assoc]
  -- it never meets the branch locus
  have hmem : ∀ c, pullback.fst g p (σ c) ∈ U := by
    intro c
    by_contra hc
    have hcy : (σ ≫ pullback.fst g p) c = y := by
      have h' : pullback.fst g p (σ c) ∉ (U : Set Y) := hc
      rw [hU] at h'
      simpa using h'
    have : Etale ((σ ≫ pullback.fst g p) ≫ g) := by
      rw [Category.assoc, pullback.condition, ← Category.assoc, hσ]
      infer_instance
    have : IsLocallyNoetherian C.toScheme := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian C.ι
    exact false_of_etale_comp_of_eq g (σ ≫ pullback.fst g p) c y hcy hram hnf
  -- its image is the image of `P`, hence closed, and it is open
  have hrange : Set.range σ = Φ '' P := by
    ext z
    constructor
    · rintro ⟨c, rfl⟩
      refine ⟨PO.ι ((φ ⁻¹ᵁ C).ι (inv (φ ∣_ C) c)), (((φ ⁻¹ᵁ C).ι (inv (φ ∣_ C) c))).2, ?_⟩
      simp only [hσdef, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply]
    · rintro ⟨c, hcP, rfl⟩
      let c' : (φ ⁻¹ᵁ C).toScheme := ⟨⟨c, hcP⟩, hPE hcP⟩
      have hc' : inv (φ ∣_ C) ((φ ∣_ C) c') = c' := by
        rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, IsIso.hom_inv_id]
        rfl
      refine ⟨(φ ∣_ C) c', ?_⟩
      simp only [hσdef, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hc']
      rfl
  have hclosed : IsClosed (Set.range σ) := hrange ▸ Φ.isClosedMap _ hP.isClosed
  have hopen : IsOpen (Set.range σ) := isOpen_range_of_mem g U p (C.ι ≫ q) σ hσ hmem
  -- it therefore contains the part over the component of `q w'`, which meets `y`
  have hE := h (q w') hw'
  let w'C : C.toScheme := ⟨w', mem_connectedComponent⟩
  have hσw : pullback.snd g p (σ w'C) = q w' := by
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hσ]
    rfl
  have hsubset := hE.subset_isClopen ⟨hclosed, hopen⟩
    ⟨σ w'C, by simp only [Set.mem_preimage, hσw, mem_connectedComponent], Set.mem_range_self _⟩
  obtain ⟨zy, hzy1, hzy2⟩ :=
    Scheme.Pullback.exists_preimage_pullback (f := g) (g := p) y (q w') (hgy.trans hw'.symm)
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hsubset (show zy ∈ (pullback.snd g p) ⁻¹' connectedComponent (q w') by
    simp only [Set.mem_preimage, hzy2, mem_connectedComponent])
  have := hmem c
  rw [hc, hzy1] at this
  have h' : y ∈ (U : Set Y) := this
  rw [hU] at h'
  exact h' rfl

end FiniteEtaleStep

section Assembly

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Y ⟶ X) (U : Y.Opens) {x : X} {u y : Y}

/-- A single open immersion or finite étale morphism is étale. -/
theorem etale_of_step {W W' : Scheme.{u}} (q : W' ⟶ W)
    (hq : (@IsOpenImmersion ⊔ (@IsFinite ⊓ @Etale) : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) q) :
    Etale q := by
  rcases hq with hq | hq
  · have : IsOpenImmersion q := hq
    infer_instance
  · exact hq.2

/-- **The finite étale step.** If the invariant holds for `p : W ⟶ X` and `q : W' ⟶ W` is
finite étale, it holds for `q ≫ p`. Otherwise the part of `Y ×_X W'` over a connected component
of `W'` splits into two open and closed pieces; both surject onto the component, so each
contains exactly one of the two points over a point `w'` above `x`, and the piece containing
the point over `u` contradicts `false_of_isClopen_piece`. -/
theorem preconnectedOverComponent_comp_finite_etale (hU : (U : Set Y) = {y}ᶜ) (hgy : g y = x)
    (hfib : g ⁻¹' {x} = {u, y}) (hbiju : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap u).hom)
    (hbijy : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap y).hom) (huy : u ≠ y)
    [Etale (U.ι ≫ g)] [Flat g] [IsFinite g] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (hram : Ideal.map (g.stalkMap y).hom (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))) ≤
      maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ^ 2)
    (hnf : ¬ IsField (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))) [IsAlgClosed (X.residueField x)]
    {W W' : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) [Etale p] (q : W' ⟶ W) [IsFinite q] [Etale q]
    (h : PreconnectedOverComponent g x p) : PreconnectedOverComponent g x (q ≫ p) := by
  intro w' hw'
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian W' := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (q ≫ p)
  set E' := (pullback.snd g (q ≫ p)) ⁻¹' connectedComponent w' with hE'
  have hE'c : IsClopen E' :=
    isClopen_connectedComponent.preimage (pullback.snd g (q ≫ p)).continuous
  have hover : ∀ c, pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) c = w' →
      pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) c = u ∨ pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) c = y := by
    intro c hc
    have : pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) c ∈ g ⁻¹' {x} := by
      simp only [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff, pullback_condition_apply, hc]
      exact hw'
    rw [hfib] at this
    simpa using this
  have huniq : ∀ c₁ c₂, pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) c₁ = w' → pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) c₂ = w' →
      pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) c₁ = pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) c₂ → c₁ = c₂ := by
    intro c₁ c₂ h₁ h₂ hf
    refine pullback_point_eq c₁ c₂ hf (h₁.trans h₂.symm) ?_
    rcases hover c₂ h₂ with h | h <;> rw [h] <;> assumption
  have hpiece : ∀ P, IsClopen P → P ⊆ E' → P.Nonempty →
      ∃ c ∈ P, pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) c = w' := by
    rintro P hP hPE ⟨c₀, hc₀⟩
    have hcl : IsClopen (pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) '' P) :=
      ⟨(pullback.snd g (q ≫ p)).isClosedMap _ hP.isClosed,
        (pullback.snd g (q ≫ p)).isOpenMap _ hP.isOpen⟩
    have hsub := hcl.connectedComponent_subset (Set.mem_image_of_mem _ hc₀)
    rw [← connectedComponent_eq (hPE hc₀)] at hsub
    exact hsub mem_connectedComponent
  have hsplit : ∀ (Q : Set ↥(pullback g (q ≫ p))) (d e : ↥(pullback g (q ≫ p))), d ∈ Q → e ∉ Q →
      pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) d = w' → pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) e = w' →
      pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) d ≠ pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) e →
      ∀ c ∈ Q, pullback.snd g (q ≫ p) c = w' → c = d := by
    intro Q d e hd he hdw hew hde c hc hcw
    by_cases hcd : pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) c = pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) d
    · exact huniq c d hcw hdw hcd
    · have hce : pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) c = pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) e := by
        rcases hover c hcw with h1 | h1 <;> rcases hover d hdw with h2 | h2 <;>
          rcases hover e hew with h3 | h3
        all_goals first
          | exact h1.trans h3.symm
          | exact absurd (h1.trans h2.symm) hcd
          | exact absurd (h2.trans h3.symm) hde
      exact absurd (huniq c e hcw hew hce ▸ hc) he
  by_contra hnc
  rw [isPreconnected_closed_iff] at hnc
  push Not at hnc
  obtain ⟨t₁, t₂, ht₁, ht₂, hcov, hne₁, hne₂, hdisj⟩ := hnc
  have hdisj' : ∀ z, z ∈ E' → z ∈ t₁ → z ∈ t₂ → False := fun z hz h1 h2 =>
    (Set.eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem.mp hdisj) z ⟨hz, h1, h2⟩
  have hA : IsClopen (E' ∩ t₁) := by
    refine ⟨hE'c.isClosed.inter ht₁, ?_⟩
    have : E' ∩ t₁ = E' ∩ t₂ᶜ := by
      ext z
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨hz, h1⟩
        exact ⟨hz, fun h2 => hdisj' z hz h1 h2⟩
      · rintro ⟨hz, h2⟩
        exact ⟨hz, (hcov hz).resolve_right h2⟩
    rw [this]
    exact hE'c.isOpen.inter ht₂.isOpen_compl
  have hB : IsClopen (E' ∩ t₂) := by
    refine ⟨hE'c.isClosed.inter ht₂, ?_⟩
    have : E' ∩ t₂ = E' ∩ t₁ᶜ := by
      ext z
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨hz, h2⟩
        exact ⟨hz, fun h1 => hdisj' z hz h1 h2⟩
      · rintro ⟨hz, h1⟩
        exact ⟨hz, (hcov hz).resolve_left h1⟩
    rw [this]
    exact hE'c.isOpen.inter ht₁.isOpen_compl
  obtain ⟨a, ⟨haE, hat⟩, haw⟩ := hpiece _ hA Set.inter_subset_left hne₁
  obtain ⟨b, ⟨hbE, hbt⟩, hbw⟩ := hpiece _ hB Set.inter_subset_left hne₂
  have hbA : b ∉ E' ∩ t₁ := fun hb => hdisj' b hbE hb.2 hbt
  have haB : a ∉ E' ∩ t₂ := fun ha => hdisj' a haE hat ha.2
  have hab : pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) a ≠ pullback.fst g (q ≫ p) b := fun hf =>
    hbA (huniq a b haw hbw hf ▸ ⟨haE, hat⟩)
  rcases hover a haw with hau | hay
  · exact false_of_isClopen_piece g U hU hgy hram hnf p q h w' hw' _ hA Set.inter_subset_left a
      ⟨haE, hat⟩ haw (by rw [hau]; exact huy) (hsplit _ a b ⟨haE, hat⟩ hbA haw hbw hab)
  · exact false_of_isClopen_piece g U hU hgy hram hnf p q h w' hw' _ hB Set.inter_subset_left b
      ⟨hbE, hbt⟩ hbw (fun hby => hab (hay.trans hby.symm))
      (hsplit _ b a ⟨hbE, hbt⟩ haB hbw haw (Ne.symm hab))

/-- **One step of the tower.** -/
theorem preconnectedOverComponent_comp_of_step {k : Type u} [Field k] (πY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k))
    [Smooth πY] (hU : (U : Set Y) = {y}ᶜ) (hgy : g y = x)
    (hfib : g ⁻¹' {x} = {u, y}) (hbiju : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap u).hom)
    (hbijy : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap y).hom) (huy : u ≠ y)
    [Etale (U.ι ≫ g)] [Flat g] [IsFinite g] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (hram : Ideal.map (g.stalkMap y).hom (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))) ≤
      maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ^ 2)
    (hnf : ¬ IsField (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))) [IsAlgClosed (X.residueField x)]
    {W W' : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X) [Etale p] [IsNoetherian W] (q : W' ⟶ W)
    (hq : (@IsOpenImmersion ⊔ (@IsFinite ⊓ @Etale) : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u}) q)
    (h : PreconnectedOverComponent g x p) : PreconnectedOverComponent g x (q ≫ p) := by
  rcases hq with hq | hq
  · have : IsOpenImmersion q := hq
    exact preconnectedOverComponent_comp_isOpenImmersion g x πY p q h
  · have : IsFinite q := hq.1
    have : Etale q := hq.2
    exact preconnectedOverComponent_comp_finite_etale g U hU hgy hfib hbiju hbijy huy hram hnf
      p q h

/-- **The invariant holds along the tower.** -/
theorem preconnectedOverComponent_of_zariskiFiniteEtaleTower {k : Type u} [Field k]
    (πY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of k)) [Smooth πY] (hU : (U : Set Y) = {y}ᶜ) (hgy : g y = x)
    (hfib : g ⁻¹' {x} = {u, y}) (hbiju : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap u).hom)
    (hbijy : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap y).hom) (huy : u ≠ y)
    [Etale (U.ι ≫ g)] [Flat g] [IsFinite g] [IsLocallyNoetherian X]
    (hram : Ideal.map (g.stalkMap y).hom (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))) ≤
      maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ^ 2)
    (hnf : ¬ IsField (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))) [IsAlgClosed (X.residueField x)]
    {A B : Scheme.{u}} {f : A ⟶ B} (hf : zariskiFiniteEtaleTower f) :
    ∀ (b : B ⟶ X) [Etale b] [IsNoetherian B], PreconnectedOverComponent g x b →
      PreconnectedOverComponent g x (f ≫ b) := by
  induction hf with
  | of f₀ hf₀ =>
    intro b _ _ hb
    exact preconnectedOverComponent_comp_of_step g U πY hU hgy hfib hbiju hbijy huy hram hnf
      b f₀ hf₀ hb
  | id A₀ =>
    intro b _ _ hb
    simpa using hb
  | comp_of f₀ g₀ _ hg₀ ih =>
    intro b _ _ hb
    have : Etale g₀ := etale_of_step g₀ hg₀
    have := isNoetherian_of_step g₀ hg₀
    rw [Category.assoc]
    exact ih (g₀ ≫ b) (preconnectedOverComponent_comp_of_step g U πY hU hgy hfib hbiju hbijy huy
      hram hnf b g₀ hg₀ hb)

/-- **The top of the tower.** If the invariant holds for `p : W ⟶ X` and `p` lifts to `U`, then
no point of `W` lies over `x`: the lift is a section of `Y ×_X W ⟶ W` whose image is open and
closed and misses every point over `y`, while the part of `Y ×_X W` over the component of a point
over `x` is preconnected and contains such a point. -/
theorem false_of_lift (hU : (U : Set Y) = {y}ᶜ) (hgy : g y = x) [FormallyUnramified (U.ι ≫ g)]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType (U.ι ≫ g)] [IsFinite g] {W : Scheme.{u}} (p : W ⟶ X)
    (h : PreconnectedOverComponent g x p) (s : W ⟶ U) (hs : s ≫ U.ι ≫ g = p) (w : W)
    (hw : p w = x) : False := by
  have hcond : (s ≫ U.ι) ≫ g = 𝟙 W ≫ p := by simpa using hs
  set σ := pullback.lift (s ≫ U.ι) (𝟙 W) hcond
  have hσ : σ ≫ pullback.snd g p = 𝟙 W := pullback.lift_snd _ _ _
  have hσf : σ ≫ pullback.fst g p = s ≫ U.ι := pullback.lift_fst _ _ _
  have : IsClosedImmersion σ :=
    isClosedImmersion_of_isSection_of_isSeparated (pullback.snd g p) σ hσ
  have hclosed : IsClosed (Set.range σ) := σ.isClosedEmbedding.isClosed_range
  have hmem : ∀ c, pullback.fst g p (σ c) ∈ U := fun c => by
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hσf, Scheme.Hom.comp_apply]
    exact (s c).2
  have hopen := isOpen_range_of_mem g U p (𝟙 W) σ hσ hmem
  have hσw : pullback.snd g p (σ w) = w := by
    rw [← Scheme.Hom.comp_apply, hσ]
    rfl
  have hsubset := (h w hw).subset_isClopen ⟨hclosed, hopen⟩
    ⟨σ w, by simp only [Set.mem_preimage, hσw, mem_connectedComponent], Set.mem_range_self _⟩
  obtain ⟨zy, hzy1, hzy2⟩ :=
    Scheme.Pullback.exists_preimage_pullback (f := g) (g := p) y w (hgy.trans hw.symm)
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hsubset (show zy ∈ (pullback.snd g p) ⁻¹' connectedComponent w by
    simp only [Set.mem_preimage, hzy2, mem_connectedComponent])
  have := hmem c
  rw [hc, hzy1] at this
  have h' : y ∈ (U : Set Y) := this
  rw [hU] at h'
  exact h' rfl

end Assembly

section Curve

variable {X Y : Scheme.{0}} {πX : X ⟶ Spec (.of ℂ)} {πY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of ℂ)}
  [IsCurve ℂ πX] [Smooth πX] [IsCurve ℂ πY] [Smooth πY]
  {g : Y ⟶ X} [IsFinite g] [IsDominant g] {x : X} {u y : Y}

omit [Smooth πX] [Smooth πY] in
include πX πY in
/-- In the source's setup, `x` is not the generic point of `X`: the generic fibre of the finite
dominant morphism `g` is the single generic point of `Y`, whereas `g⁻¹(x)` has two points. -/
theorem ne_genericPoint_of_fiber (huy : u ≠ y) (hfib : g ⁻¹' {x} = {u, y}) :
    x ≠ genericPoint X := by
  rintro rfl
  have h := preimage_genericPoint_of_isFinite_of_isDominant g
  rw [hfib] at h
  have hu : u ∈ ({genericPoint Y} : Set Y) := h ▸ Set.mem_insert u {y}
  have hy : y ∈ ({genericPoint Y} : Set Y) := h ▸ Set.mem_insert_of_mem u rfl
  exact huy ((Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp hu).trans (Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp hy).symm)

omit [Smooth πX] [Smooth πY] in
include πX πY in
/-- A point of `Y` over `x` is not the generic point of `Y`. -/
theorem ne_genericPoint_of_map (huy : u ≠ y) (hfib : g ⁻¹' {x} = {u, y}) {z : Y} (hz : g z = x) :
    z ≠ genericPoint Y := by
  rintro rfl
  exact ne_genericPoint_of_fiber (πX := πX) (πY := πY) huy hfib
    (hz.symm.trans (map_genericPoint_of_isDominant g))

end Curve

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0HAR**, pointwise form: no finite composition of open immersions and
finite étale morphisms that lifts to `U` has a point over `x`.

Here `X` is a smooth affine curve over `ℂ`, `g : Y ⟶ X` a finite morphism of degree `3` from a
smooth curve with `g⁻¹(x) = {u, y}`, `u` unramified and `y` ramified of index `2`, `g`
unramified away from `y`, and `U = Y ∖ {y}`. -/
theorem not_mem_range_of_zariskiFiniteEtaleTower {X Y : Scheme.{0}} (πX : X ⟶ Spec (.of ℂ))
    (πY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of ℂ)) [IsCurve ℂ πX] [Smooth πX] [IsAffine X] [IsCurve ℂ πY] [Smooth πY]
    (g : Y ⟶ X) (hg : g ≫ πX = πY) [IsFinite g] [IsDominant g]
    (x : X) (u y : Y) (huy : u ≠ y) (hfib : g ⁻¹' {x} = {u, y})
    (hy2 : letI := (g.stalkMap y).hom.toAlgebra
      Stacks.DiscreteValuationRing.Ramification.ramificationIdx (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))
        (Y.presheaf.stalk y) = 2)
    (U : Y.Opens) (hU : (U : Set Y) = {y}ᶜ) (hunr : FormallyUnramified (U.ι ≫ g))
    {W : Scheme.{0}} (p : W ⟶ X) (hp : zariskiFiniteEtaleTower p) (s : W ⟶ U)
    (hs : s ≫ U.ι ≫ g = p) : x ∉ Set.range p := by
  rintro ⟨w, hw⟩
  have hgu : g u = x := by
    have : u ∈ g ⁻¹' {x} := by rw [hfib]; exact Set.mem_insert u {y}
    exact this
  have hgy : g y = x := by
    have : y ∈ g ⁻¹' {x} := by rw [hfib]; exact Set.mem_insert_of_mem u rfl
    exact this
  -- the points `x`, `u`, `y` are closed
  have hxη := ne_genericPoint_of_fiber (πX := πX) (πY := πY) huy hfib
  have hxc : IsClosed ({x} : Set X) :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleDimensionOne.isClosed_singleton_of_ne_genericPoint X
      (IsCurve.topologicalKrullDim_eq_one (k := ℂ) (f := πX)) hxη
  have hyη := ne_genericPoint_of_map (πX := πX) (πY := πY) huy hfib hgy
  have huη := ne_genericPoint_of_map (πX := πX) (πY := πY) huy hfib hgu
  have hyc : IsClosed ({y} : Set Y) :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleDimensionOne.isClosed_singleton_of_ne_genericPoint Y
      (IsCurve.topologicalKrullDim_eq_one (k := ℂ) (f := πY)) hyη
  have huc : IsClosed ({u} : Set Y) :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleDimensionOne.isClosed_singleton_of_ne_genericPoint Y
      (IsCurve.topologicalKrullDim_eq_one (k := ℂ) (f := πY)) huη
  -- residue fields
  have : IsAlgClosed (X.residueField x) := isAlgClosed_residueField_of_isClosed πX x hxc
  have hbiju : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap u).hom :=
    residueFieldMap_bijective_of_isClosed πX πY g hg u huc (by rw [hgu]; exact hxc)
  have hbijy : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap y).hom :=
    residueFieldMap_bijective_of_isClosed πX πY g hg y hyc (by rw [hgy]; exact hxc)
  -- flatness and étaleness away from `y`
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian X := LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian πX
  have : IsNoetherian X := { }
  have : IsNormal X := isNormal_of_smooth_over_field πX
  have hrange : (Set.range g).Nontrivial :=
    ⟨x, ⟨u, hgu⟩, genericPoint X, ⟨genericPoint Y, map_genericPoint_of_isDominant g⟩, hxη⟩
  have : Flat g :=
    (Flat.iff_flat_stalkMap g).2 (isFlat_of_nonconstant_of_isNormal πY πX g hg hrange)
  have : FormallyUnramified (U.ι ≫ g) := hunr
  have : Etale (U.ι ≫ g) := Etale.of_formallyUnramified_of_flat (U.ι ≫ g)
  -- the ramification at `y`
  have hgyη : g y ≠ genericPoint X := hgy ▸ hxη
  have : IsDiscreteValuationRing (X.presheaf.stalk (g y)) :=
    IsCurve.isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk ℂ πX hgyη
  have : IsDiscreteValuationRing (Y.presheaf.stalk y) :=
    IsCurve.isDiscreteValuationRing_stalk ℂ πY hyη
  have hnf : ¬ IsField (X.presheaf.stalk (g y)) := IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_isField _
  have hram : Ideal.map (g.stalkMap y).hom (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))) ≤
      maximalIdeal (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ^ 2 := by
    let : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk (g y)) (Y.presheaf.stalk y) := (g.stalkMap y).hom.toAlgebra
    have hinj : ∀ z : Y, Function.Injective (g.stalkMap z) :=
      ((tfae_isDominant_of_isIntegral g).out 1 6).mp ‹IsDominant g›
    have : FaithfulSMul (X.presheaf.stalk (g y)) (Y.presheaf.stalk y) :=
      (faithfulSMul_iff_algebraMap_injective (X.presheaf.stalk (g y)) (Y.presheaf.stalk y)).mpr
        (hinj y)
    have h :=
      Stacks.DiscreteValuationRing.Ramification.map_maximalIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal_pow_ramificationIdx
        (X.presheaf.stalk (g y)) (Y.presheaf.stalk y)
    rw [hy2] at h
    exact h.le
  -- the invariant along the tower, and the contradiction at its top
  have hp' : PreconnectedOverComponent g x (p ≫ 𝟙 X) :=
    preconnectedOverComponent_of_zariskiFiniteEtaleTower g U πY hU hgy hfib hbiju hbijy huy hram hnf
      hp (𝟙 X) (preconnectedOverComponent_id g x)
  rw [Category.comp_id] at hp'
  exact false_of_lift g U hU hgy p hp' s hs w hw

end AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleNotZariskiFiniteEtale

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

open EtaleNotZariskiFiniteEtale

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0HAR.** Let `X` be a smooth connected affine curve over `ℂ` and
`g : Y ⟶ X` a finite morphism of degree `3` from a smooth connected curve `Y` over `ℂ`, such that
for some point `x` of `X` the fibre `g⁻¹(x) = {u, y}` consists of an unramified point `u`
(ramification index `1`) and a ramified point `y` (ramification index `2`), and such that `g` is
unramified everywhere except at `y`. Put `U = Y ∖ {y}`. Then the étale cover `U ⟶ X` cannot be
refined by any finite composition of open immersions and finite étale morphisms: there is no
family of finite compositions `W i ⟶ X` of open immersions and finite étale morphisms, each
factoring through `U`, which is jointly surjective.

The degree of `g` is `deg(Y/X)` of [Stacks, Tag 02NY] (`AlgebraicGeometry.degreeOver`), the
ramification indices are those of the local rings
(`Stacks.DiscreteValuationRing.Ramification.ramificationIdx`), and "unramified away from `y`" is
formal unramifiedness of the restriction of `g` to `U`. The finite compositions are the
multiplicative closure of the class of open immersions and finite étale morphisms. -/
@[stacks 0HAR]
theorem not_exists_cover_zariskiFiniteEtale_lift {X Y : Scheme.{0}} (πX : X ⟶ Spec (.of ℂ))
    (πY : Y ⟶ Spec (.of ℂ)) [IsCurve ℂ πX] [Smooth πX] [IsAffine X] [IsCurve ℂ πY] [Smooth πY]
    (g : Y ⟶ X) (hg : g ≫ πX = πY) [IsFinite g] [IsDominant g] (_hdeg : degreeOver g = 3)
    (x : X) (u y : Y) (huy : u ≠ y) (hfib : g ⁻¹' {x} = {u, y})
    (_hu1 : letI := (g.stalkMap u).hom.toAlgebra
      Stacks.DiscreteValuationRing.Ramification.ramificationIdx (X.presheaf.stalk (g u))
        (Y.presheaf.stalk u) = 1)
    (hy2 : letI := (g.stalkMap y).hom.toAlgebra
      Stacks.DiscreteValuationRing.Ramification.ramificationIdx (X.presheaf.stalk (g y))
        (Y.presheaf.stalk y) = 2)
    (U : Y.Opens) (hU : (U : Set Y) = {y}ᶜ) (hunr : FormallyUnramified (U.ι ≫ g)) :
    ¬ ∃ (ι : Type) (W : ι → Scheme.{0}) (p : ∀ i, W i ⟶ X),
      (∀ i, (@IsOpenImmersion ⊔ (@IsFinite ⊓ @Etale) :
        MorphismProperty Scheme.{0}).multiplicativeClosure (p i)) ∧
      (∀ i, ∃ s : W i ⟶ U, s ≫ U.ι ≫ g = p i) ∧ ⋃ i, Set.range (p i) = Set.univ := by
  rintro ⟨ι, W, p, hp, hlift, hcov⟩
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.mp (hcov ▸ Set.mem_univ x : x ∈ ⋃ i, Set.range (p i))
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := hlift i
  exact not_mem_range_of_zariskiFiniteEtaleTower πX πY g hg x u y huy hfib hy2 U hU hunr (p i)
    (hp i) s hs hi

end AlgebraicGeometry
